From b7c7ed978f04bea20a4c6abbf763d31940142e60 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Cruslan <147114339+Cruslan@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 30 Sep 2026 02:15:30 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] librsx, cgcomp: Fix RSX GPU hangs, pointer arithmetic
 overflows, and texcoords handling

- Fix pointer scaling overflow in rsxSetupContextData by casting addr to uintptr_t before adding byte length.
- Add allowTex (bit 15) flag in compilerfp.cpp and LoadFragmentProgramLocation when fragment program samples textures.
- Correct SetVertexProgramConstants second burst source offset to &value[16] instead of value.
- Fix SetTimeStamp writing outside allocated packet bounds (currenp[1] instead of [2]).
- Fix ResetCommandBuffer to query real buffer start offset via gcmAddressToOffset and rewind context->current.
- Fix rsxContextCallback assembly calling convention to preserve registers across 32-bit OPD invocations.
- Add missing vdec codec defines in vdec.h.
